+# Review repairs — targeted handback
+
+The review repairs are ready for parent verification. **Five selected component scenarios, 32 selected Runtime tests and 10 offline checks passed.** Both selected project builds completed with zero warnings/errors. The initial repair build failure remains retained. No broad suite, deployment, serving/worker operation, native experiment or image build ran in this repair pass.
+
+The previous verification/inventory files describe the pre-review snapshot. They remain unchanged. In particular, the earlier 41-file image-context result does **not** satisfy the repaired runtime-image gate: the real publish inventory lacks an actual reviewed runtime-image pin, and the new attempt is **Blocked**. Only isolated regression fixtures contain synthetic image pins. Parent-owned full verification and a separate final reviewed inventory follow this handback.
+
+| Review repair | Implemented behavior and targeted evidence |
+| --- | --- |
+| Actor revisions versus independent custody head | Original wrap/registration/lifecycle `ExpectedRevision` and bytes remain actor-owned. Fresh envelope/proof custody revision still drives native current-head/digest verification and whole-head CAS. No public wire field was added. The actual `CustodyKeyLifecycleActor` test registers two roots at owner revisions 0/1 while custody starts at 7 and advances independently, then pins, unpins and recovers immutable originals through the real SDK/service boundary. |
+| Supported NotPerformed cleanup | The production authority accepts NotPerformed only when exact authenticated retained lookup equals the supplied complete original outcome. The actor test first retains a genuinely pending fixture pin, then recovers a separately retained never-performed original, rejects a substituted receipt and proves the actor removes its pending pin. No absence/never-performed synthesis was added. |
+| Explicit caller cancellation and discarded keys | Public client, credential-bound authorizer, lifecycle provider and lifecycle-authority forwarders recheck caller cancellation after lower awaits/refusals and before result exposure. Discarded owned results are cleared. Runtime tests exercise interrupted false-returning owner forwarders, a refusing credential transport, a cancelling registration locator and discarded owned-key cleanup; component tests cancel after actual key response and prove retry releases no second key. |
+| One whole-operation deadline | One shared thirty-second budget spans authorizer preparation/signing, registration lookup, manifest locator, manifest call and all pages. Unresponsive locators use that token/remaining budget. Internal expiry returns Unknown; explicit caller cancellation throws with the original caller token. Virtual-clock component tests cross registration/locator/manifest and header/page boundaries and stop later I/O at the original deadline. |
+| Real signed-response replay | The SDK bridge captures a valid signed unwrap response and replays it on a retry with the same operation/delivery but a fresh attempt/challenge. Public authentication refuses its key and the native release count remains one. |
+| Manual daprd identity, host and discovery | Review templates explicitly project the scoped Sentry token, reference public trust and both API-channel token Secrets, configure namespace/trust domain/control-plane/Sentry/mTLS, and supply actual host port/protocol. An `appId-dapr` Service selects the owning workload and exposes only the pinned mTLS internal port 50002. Offline rendered tests assert token/trust/API/host/selector/port relationships. |
+| Worker output ownership | Configured worker group is both `runAsGroup` and `fsGroup`, with `OnRootMismatch`. The storage owner must establish actual PVC/CSI group ownership and a writable exclusively created retained output beneath `/retained`. That requirement is explicit installation input. |
+| Native credential consumption | Infrastructure explicitly loads the selected mounted file/profile and passes those credentials to all three native SDK clients. The accepted profile has only access/secret and optional session-token keys; ambient/default, role/process and metadata fallback are excluded. Component/worker templates map exact Secret keys to `/credentials/credentials`, select the profile and disable metadata. Targeted tests consume a fixture session profile and deny wrong/duplicate/metadata profiles without native calls. |
+| Duplicate JSON properties | Both preflight inputs and publish inventories reject duplicate keys recursively, including conflicting nested fields. Targeted offline regressions pass. |
+| Runtime image binding | The closed hash-bound inventory now contains exact `runtimeImage` plus complete `files`. The matching immutable runtime pin is required and is emitted literally in the prepared Dockerfile; there is no overridable runtime-image build argument. Mutable, interpolated or substituted pins are rejected. The real missing-pin attempt is retained as Blocked; earlier contexts remain pre-review evidence. |
+| Evidence retention | A narrowly scoped `.gitignore` exception retains existing and future custody verification logs, including intermediate failures. The offline check confirms custody logs are unignored and an unrelated log remains ignored. |
+| Concrete locator dependencies | `source-dispositions.json`, `reference-profile-inputs.json`, deployment inputs and the new deduplicated ledger explicitly name `ICustodyKeyRegistrationSource` and `ICustodyReservedManifestSource` implementations, installation owners and exact retained full-identity/reservation mappings. EventStore owns the complete reserved-manifest original mapping; Platform custody owns the registration locator. |
+
+## Retained targeted results
+
+- `verification/review-repairs/component-build-1.log`: retained initial compile failure.
+- `verification/review-repairs/component-build-2.log`, `component-build-3.log`: successful component test-project builds.
+- `verification/review-repairs/component-targeted-tests-2.log`: five selected scenarios, zero failures: public lifecycle; actual actor/diverged revisions/NotPerformed; cancellation/shared deadline; explicit native credential selection; two-target original recovery.
+- `verification/review-repairs/runtime-build-1.log`: successful Runtime test-project build.
+- `verification/review-repairs/runtime-targeted-tests-1.log`: 32 tests from `CustodyBindingContractTests`, `CustodyLifecyclePublicContractTests` and `CustodyLifecycleCancellationTests`; zero errors/failures/skips/unrun.
+- `verification/review-repairs/offline-tests-3.log`: ten tests covering changed preflight/image preparation/rendered wiring/log-retention files, all passed.
+- `verification/review-repairs/real-image-context-missing-runtime-pin.log`: expected Blocked result, imageBuilt=false.
+- `verification/review-repairs/preflight-after-review.log` and `installation-input-ledger-after-review.json`: expected Blocked result, 68 unique missing inputs with owners/actions.
+
+Builds selected the current sibling EventStore source graph explicitly and used external artifact directories `/tmp/custody-lifecycle-review-repairs-20261025a` and `/tmp/custody-lifecycle-review-runtime-20261025a`. Only the named component scenarios and Runtime classes ran. Source-reference package-lock drift was restored to current committed bytes. Concurrent unrelated work was preserved.
